## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests understanding of partition dynamic programming with nontrivial segment costs, requiring careful recurrence formulation, efficient range query handling, and solution reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP with fixed number of contiguous segments
- Segment cost computation using range max-min queries
- Reconstruction via predecessor pointers
- Time/space optimization techniques

## Code Example
```javascript
function minCostPartitions(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(Infinity));
  const pre = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));

  dp[0][0] = 0;

  // Base case: single segment
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    let maxVal = A[0], minVal = A[0];
    for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
      maxVal = Math.max(maxVal, A[j]);
      minVal = Math.min(minVal, A[j]);
      dp[i][1] = maxVal - minVal;
    }
  }

  // DP transitions
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = t - 1; j < i; j++) {
        const segmentCost = computeCost(A, j + 1, i);
        if (dp[j][t - 1] + segmentCost < dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = dp[j][t - 1] + segmentCost;
          pre[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct segments
  const segments = [];
  let end = n;
  for (let t = k; t >= 1; t--) {
    const start = pre[end][t] + 1;
    segments.unshift([start, end]);
    end = pre[end][t];
  }

  return { minCost: dp[n][k], segments };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP design when block value is nonlinear in length and sum, forcing nontrivial transitions and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping subarrays DP, prefix sums, reconstruction pointers
- Time/space trade-offs with O(n^2 k) baseline, potential optimizations
- Handling exact k blocks and base cases

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKBlocks(A, k){
  const n=A.length; const S=[0]; for(const x of A) S.push(S[S.length-1]+x);
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1e15));
  const prv=Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0]=0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
      dp[i][t]=dp[i-1][t];
      if(t>0){
        for(let l=1;l<=i;l++){
          const sum=S[i]-S[l-1];
          const val=dp[l-1][t-1]+sum*(i-l+1);
          if(val>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; prv[i][t]=l; }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {best:dp[n][k]};
}
```

