- How does the reconstruction change if ties occur on values?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests classic DP with an additional dimension (at most k intervals) and reconstruction—a common pattern in scheduling optimization problems.

## Key Concepts
- Weighted interval scheduling with a cardinality constraint (at most k intervals)
- Predecessor p(i) computed via binary search on sorted end times
- DP table with an extra dimension tracking the number of selected intervals
- Backtracking reconstruction to output the chosen jobs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxValueKJobs(jobs, k) {
  const sorted = jobs.map((j, idx) => ({ ...j, idx })).sort((a, b) => a.end - b.end);
  const n = sorted.length;
  const ends = sorted.map(j => j.end);

  const p = (i) => {
    let lo = 0, hi = i - 1;
    while (lo <= hi) {
      const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi) / 2);
      if (ends[mid] <= sorted[i].start) lo = mid + 1;
      else hi = mid - 1;
    }
    return hi;
  };

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      const prev = p(i - 1) + 1;
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][t], dp[prev][t - 1] + sorted[i - 1].value);
    }
  }

  const selected = [];
  let t = k;
  for (let i = n; i > 0 && t > 0; i--) {
    if (dp[i][t] !== dp[i - 1][t]) {
      selected.push(sorted[i - 1]);
      t--;
    }
  }

  return { value: dp[n][k], jobs: selected.reverse() };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests DP with a non-adjacent removal constraint and requires reconstruction of which indices were removed.

## Key Concepts

- 3D DP state dp[i][t][r]
- Non-adjacent constraint during removal
- Path reconstruction for the chosen indices

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxRemainingSum(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = Number.NEGATIVE_INFINITY / 4;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () =>
    Array.from({ length: k + 1 }, () => [NEG, NEG])
  );
  dp[0][0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      // keep i
      dp[i][t][0] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t][0], dp[i-1][t][1]) + A[i-1];
      // remove i
      if (t > 0) dp[i][t][1] = dp[i-1][t-1][0];
    }
  }
  return Math.max(dp[n][k][0], dp[n][k][1]);
}
```

